/**
 * @file SepiaFactoryPackTests.cpp
 * @brief Holds the bundled factory preset pack to what it promises a player.
 *
 * The pack is generated by tools/sepia-presets/build_pack.py. These tests read the archive the
 * app ships, load it the way the app does, and play each preset through a real controller:
 *
 *   - the archive is self-contained: no model, IR or other resource, in the archive or on a node
 *   - every node is a registered effect and every parameter is one it has, within range
 *   - names are unique, and none borrows an artist's, a song's or another product's
 *   - a controller with the archive bundled offers its presets by id
 *   - every preset is as loud as the others on three kinds of playing, and never clips
 *   - the Metal group really is high gain, and the clean group really is clean
 *   - a high-gain chain opens with a noise gate, and is silent with nothing plugged in
 *   - changing preset mid-note does not click
 *
 * `--measure <file>` writes each preset's levels as JSON for tools/sepia-presets/level.py and
 * skips the level checks, which is how the pack is level-matched in the first place.
 */

